flowchart TB
    accTitle: How the two jobs share the runs
    accDescr: run-all.sh splits the runs of the suite into two shards, one for each required check, which runs its runs side by side on a runner of its own. Shard 1, the check nextcloud, holds the oldest and the newest supported version; shard 2, the check nextcloud on PostgreSQL, MariaDB and S3, holds the newest version on PostgreSQL and on MariaDB with S3, when the change can behave differently there. Each version between goes, from the oldest, to the shard with the lighter load, where a version with its browser checks counts as two runs and a variant as one, and to shard 2 when both weigh as much. With Nextcloud 33 to 35, shard 1 runs 33 and 35 and shard 2 runs 34 and both variants.

    all["run-all.sh<br>E2E_SHARD"]
    between{"each version<br>between, from<br>the oldest"}
    first["shard 1, nextcloud:<br>the oldest and the<br>newest version"]
    second["shard 2, nextcloud on<br>PostgreSQL, MariaDB<br>and S3: the newest<br>version there"]
    example["Nextcloud 33 to 35:<br>33 and 35 in shard 1,<br>34 and both<br>variants in shard 2"]

    all --> first
    all --> second
    all --> between
    between -- "shard 2 weighs<br>less or as much:<br>a version 2,<br>a variant 1" --> second
    between -- "shard 1<br>weighs less" --> first
    first ~~~ example
    second ~~~ example

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class all,between bot
    class first,second,example done
